@flexiarg operator/grant-the-go-ahead
@title Grant the Go-Ahead (existing proposal, 9 prior occurrences — RIPE, no draft written)
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 3 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-KEC8y8 turn-UQbEZV turn-nfzNqt; first proposed for: The agent has paused mid-work — turn ended, question asked, or permission implied — and the operator wants it to keep going on the course already set.
@why [orchestration/consent-gate]

! conclusion: Grant continuation in its minimal form ('OK, please continue') — acknowledge the state, hand the momentum back, add nothing.

  + IF:
    The current course is already agreed and the only thing missing is licence to proceed.

  + HOWEVER:
    a bare go-ahead carries no steering information, so it is exactly wrong when the operator actually wants a course correction smuggled in; but when the course is right, anything longer is friction.

  + THEN:
    Grant continuation in its minimal form ('OK, please continue') — acknowledge the state, hand the momentum back, add nothing.

  + BECAUSE:
    It is the operator-side utterance at a consent point: the minimal recorded approval that lets the agent act, specialised to the reversible/in-scope case where no formal gate artifact is warranted.
